SUMMARY:Remembrance Day Event at the Region of Peel Archives
DESCRIPTION:Peel Remembers: \nA Legacy of Service and Sacrifice \nThursday\, November 5\, 4:00 p.m. – 8:00 p.m.\nSaturday\, November 7\, 10:00 a.m. – 4:00 p.m. \nTo commemorate Remembrance Day\, join archivists in this drop-in event to remember the service and sacrifices of Peel residents. From the War of 1812 to the Cold War\, discover stories preserved in letters\, photographs\, war posters\, and other archival records that highlight moments of conflict across almost two centuries. \nAdmission to the Archives is free. Access to PAMA’s Museum and Art Gallery is also available with purchase of admission.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/remembrance-day-event-at-the-region-of-peel-archives/2026-11-07/
LOCATION:Peel Art Gallery\, Museum & Archives (PAMA)\, 9 Wellington Street East\, Brampton\, ON\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Region of Peel Archives":MAILTO:archives@peelregion.ca
END:VEVENT
