SUMMARY:Thornhill Historical Society: Inaugural Thornhill Remembrance Day Ceremony
DESCRIPTION:Join us as Thornhill gathers for its first official community Remembrance Day service on the grounds of the historic 1950 Living War Memorial. \nA LIVING MEMORIAL BORN OF COMMUNITY SPIRIT: \nOn June 16\, 1950\, the Thornhill Community Memorial and Recreation Centre was dedicated as a living memorial to the men and women who served in the two World Wars. Originally proposed by Gordon C. Leitch and championed by the Thornhill Lions Club\, the facility featured war memorial tablets donated by the Thornhill Women’s Institute. These were unveiled by two bereaved mothers – Mrs. William Riddell (World War I) and Mrs. Roy Wice (World War II). The pool was intended to be a Living Memorial to honour the fallen through the health and vitality of local youth during peacetime. This November 11\, we will gather to reaffirm this solemn commitment and pay tribute to our local heroes. \nWe hope to see you on Wednesday\, November 11th at 10:45AM\, when we will especially remember those Thornhill residents who fought for our freedom and democracy\, as well as those who paid the ultimate sacrifice and could not return home to their families. 
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/thornhill-historical-society-inaugural-thornhill-remembrance-day-ceremony/
LOCATION:Thornhill Swimming Pool Grounds\, 26 Old Yonge St.\, Thornhill\, ON\, L4J 1E9\, Canada
END:VEVENT
