SUMMARY:Guelph Black Heritage Society: War and Peace: Songs and Monologues
DESCRIPTION:As part of this season of remembrance\, we invite you to experience War and Peace: Songs and Monologues. \n2 Showings: \n\n1:00 p.m.\n7:30 p.m.\n\nNovember 11th\, 2026 \nGuelph Little Theatre\, 176 Morris Street\, Guelph \nPresented by Culchahworks in partnership with the Guelph Black Heritage Society and Guelph Museums. \nFeaturing powerful music and thought-provoking storytelling\, Artistic Director Andrew Craig (Rhapsodius) explores questions about conflict\, peace\, and our shared humanity through songs by artists including Stevie Wonder\, Marvin Gaye\, Bob Dylan\, John Lennon\, and Bob Marley.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/guelph-black-heritage-society-war-and-peace-songs-and-monologues/2026-11-11/1/
LOCATION:Guelph Little Theatre\, 176 Morris Street\, Guelph\, ON\, N1E 5M7\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Guelph Black Heritage Society":MAILTO:marketing.gbhs@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
