UID:10002822-1794652200-1794668400@ontariohistoricalsociety.ca
SUMMARY:The Sororum Presents: A Step Through Time
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, November 14th\, join us in the heart of Yorkville as we step into a world of history\, art\, and craftsmanship. \n\n\n\n\nOur journey begins at the iconic Bata Shoe Museum\, housed within Raymond Moriyama’s award-winning architectural landmark. Here\, we’ll uncover fascinating stories of craftsmanship\, culture\, and human expression before enjoying a hands-on creative experience. \nFrom the museum\, we’ll make our way to the historic Oxley for an intimate lunch and engaging conversation\, bringing together the elements that make every Sororum gathering special: discovery\, meaningful dialogue\, and the joy of connecting with extraordinary women. \nHow Our Day Will Unfold\n10:30 AM – 12:15 PM | Private Guided Museum Tour \nWe’ll begin with a private guided exploration of two remarkable exhibitions\, each revealing how something as familiar as footwear can tell extraordinary stories about the people\, cultures\, and civilizations that came before us. \n\nUnearthing Vindolanda: Footwear from the Edge of the Roman Empire — Step back nearly 2\,000 years and discover remarkably preserved footwear offering a rare and intimate glimpse into everyday life along the northern frontier of the Roman Empire.\nBrilliant: The Art of Beaded Footwear Around the World — Journey across cultures and generations to discover the beauty\, symbolism\, and extraordinary artistry of beadwork\, and the stories of identity\, tradition\, and craftsmanship woven into every creation.\n\n12:15 PM – 1:00 PM | A Hands-On Leatherworking Experience \nFrom appreciating craftsmanship to trying our hand at it! \nWe’ll learn about traditional leatherworking techniques before creating our very own custom leather keychain — a beautiful little keepsake to remember the day. \n1:15 PM – 3:00 PM | Lunch & Guided Discussion at The Oxley \nAt the heart of every Sororum gathering is the opportunity to connect\, share perspectives\, and enjoy thoughtful conversation. \nWe’ll continue our afternoon at The Oxley\, a charming British-inspired restaurant nestled within a late-19th-century Victorian townhouse in Yorkville. With its old-world character and inviting atmosphere\, it provides a wonderful setting to gather around the table. \nOver a specially arranged prix fixe lunch\, we’ll enjoy delicious food\, warm company\, and a guided discussion inspired by the stories and discoveries of our morning together. \n3:00 PM Onward | Discover Yorkville \nFor those wishing to extend the day\, Yorkville awaits! \nEnjoy an afternoon exploring one of Toronto’s most charming neighbourhoods\, where historic Victorian streetscapes meet art galleries\, inviting cafés\, and beautiful boutiques. A lovely opportunity to linger\, explore\, and enjoy the autumn atmosphere at your own pace. \nEvent Details & Pricing\nEvent Ticket: $75 per person \nIncludes: \n\nAdmission to the Bata Shoe Museum\nExclusive private guided museum tour\nHands-on leatherworking workshop and keepsake\nFacilitated group discussion at The Oxley\n\nLunch: $40 per person + applicable taxes \nThe Sororum has arranged a special prix fixe menu exclusively for our group. Lunch is paid individually by each guest at the restaurant and is not included in the event ticket. \nMore Than an Outing. A Shared Experience.\nAt The Sororum\, we believe the most memorable experiences are those that inspire curiosity\, spark meaningful conversation\, and bring women together. \nA Step Through Time is an invitation to discover something new\, celebrate the artistry and stories of those who came before us\, and create a few wonderful memories of our own. \nWe look forward to sharing this special day with you.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/the-sororum-presents-a-step-through-time/
LOCATION:Bata Shoe Museum\, 327 Bloor St W\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 1W7\, Canada
END:VEVENT
