SUMMARY:Historical Society of Ottawa - Songs of Old Bytown—Exploring History Through Fiction
DESCRIPTION:Guest Speaker: Lawrence P. O’Brien\, Author\, Swallowing the Muskellunge \nDetails \nCreating a work of historical fiction\, drawn from the Ottawa-Gatineau area’s past\, Lawrence O’Brien re-imagines the journey that might have been made here by the Ottawa Valley’s first Black settler\, London Oxford\, and his family. \nThe resulting novel blends action\, adventure… and ventures into the supernatural. \nAdmission is free. All are welcome to attend.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/historical-society-of-ottawa-songs-of-old-bytown-exploring-history-through-fiction/
LOCATION:Ottawa Public Library\, Main Branch\, 120 Metcalfe St.\, Ottawa\, Ontario\, K1P 5M2\, Canada
